    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d381-a2">

                <pb facs="0455" n="395" sameAs="frus:frus1895p1/pg395"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 2 in No. 89.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mrs. Waller to Mr.
                            Wetter</hi>.</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Antananarivo</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1895-01-28"><hi rendition="#italic">January 28,
                        1895</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Dear Sir</hi>: As I have been in constant anxiety
                    about Mr. Waller being detained in Tamatave, as his health has not been good for
                    the past year, I now write and inclose to you a petition from friends,
                    accompanied by my earnest request that you will allow my husband to return to
                    Antananarivo, where the money to pay the judgment can be raised, if he is here
                    in person.</p>
                <p>I have twice succeeded in raising the money, but was defeated at the last moment
                    on account of my not having a proper power of attorney to sign my husband’s name
                    to the documents made. Some of the men were willing to accept my signature, but
                    the British vice-consul refused to register the contract unless I had the right
                    power of attorney. These men desire Mr. Waller to come to Antananarivo, and he
                    may sign and make the contract himself. Of course you are aware that Mr. Waller
                    can not raise the money in Tamatave, and besides, as the war is now on, his
                    family must necessarily suffer by his further detention in Tamatave.</p>
                <p>Hoping that you will grant this request, I am,</p>
                <p>Very respectfully,</p>
                <p rendition="#right">Mrs. <hi rendition="#small-caps">J. L. Waller.</hi></p>
                <p>I certify the foregoing to be an exact copy of the original on file in the office
                    of this consulate.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Edw. Telfair Wetter</hi>,<lb/><hi
                            rendition="#italic">United States Consul</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Acting</hi>).</signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
